{"requirements":[{"id":"R1","requirement":"On node1, new interactive login sessions default to umask 027.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The installed configuration specifies 027, and direct root and non-root interactive login-shell tests reported umask 0027 and created directories/files with modes 750/640. The same behavior was observed after reboot.","evidence_ids":["cmd-3b7ce64aff3a41ea","cmd-8fc14b0c85d14450","cmd-bbb5afa6d5d94f08","cmd-766efbb27d2c4e78"]}],"confidence":0.97,"operational_hygiene":{"score":0.98,"summary":"No demonstrated unnecessary mutation was found. Configuration changes directly served the outcome; temporary verification artifacts were cleaned; and the reboot served the mandatory restart protocol. cmd-3b7ce64aff3a41ea conditionally created two rollback backups whose final presence was not inventoried, but their creation had a clear bounded safety purpose. Package health remained intact, temporary-file snapshots show no task residue, and the failed SSH service existed before execution and remained unchanged.","evidence_ids":["cmd-3b7ce64aff3a41ea","cmd-e7ae8132f52f41cf","cmd-8fc14b0c85d14450","cmd-ac6b24726058402b","cmd-766efbb27d2c4e78","cmd-bbb5afa6d5d94f08","global:before_prepare:node1:temporary-files","global:after_executor:node1:temporary-files","global:before_prepare:node1:failed-services","global:after_executor:node1:failed-services","global:before_prepare:node1:package-health","global:after_executor:node1:package-health"]},"overall_summary":"The task outcome is satisfied. Runtime evidence covers root and non-root interactive login shells and confirms persistence after a completed node restart. The restart protocol includes a pre-restart identity and task-relevant baseline, acknowledgement, changed post-restart identity, and recovered targets, writable storage, configuration, and behavior; the fixed lifecycle boot identities independently corroborate the transition.","limitations":["The interactive-session tests used su with Bash -lic rather than an actual console or SSH-attached terminal, and did not exercise every installed shell.","The host was systemd-degraded because ssh.service was already failed before execution and remained failed afterward. Thus the restart evidence proves recovery of task-relevant login, target, and storage state, but not a wholly healthy host; this pre-existing condition does not reduce task functionality.","The lifecycle inventory did not cover /etc, so it does not directly establish whether the conditional rollback backups from cmd-3b7ce64aff3a41ea were newly created and retained."]}
